### Description

Using the following test data

```
{
  "mappings": {
    "properties": {
      "emp_no": {
        "type": "long"
      },
      "name": {
        "type": "keyword"
      },
      "job": {
        "type": "text",
        "fields": {
          "raw1": {
            "type": "keyword"
          },
          "raw2": {
            "type": "keyword",
            "ignore_above": 11
          }
        }
      },
      "tag": {
        "type": "text"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

```
{ "index": { } }
{ "emp_no": 10, "name": "Jenny", "job": "IT Director", "ip1": "127.0", "ip2": ".0.1" }
{ "index": { } }
{ "emp_no": 20, "name": "John", "job": "Payroll Specialist", "ip1": "127.0", "ip2": "0.1" }
{ "index": { } }
{ "emp_no": 30, "name": "John", "job": "Payroll Specialist" }
```

This query `FROM test | eval x1 = concat(ip1, ip2), x2 = coalesce(x1, \"255.255.255.255\"), x3 = to_ip(x2)` fails with 

```
"type": "verification_exception",
"reason": "Found 1 problem\nline 1:90: Unknown column [x2], did you mean [x1]?"
```

And this other one `FROM test | eval x1 = concat(ip1, ip2), x2 = coalesce(concat(ip1, ip2), \"255.255.255.255\"), x3 = to_ip(x2)` fails differently

```
        "type": "illegal_argument_exception",
        "reason": "Failed trying to format bytes as IP address.  Possibly caused by a mapping mismatch",
        "caused_by": {
            "type": "illegal_argument_exception",
            "reason": "32 > 0"
        }
```

I believe none of them should fail given the test data.
